From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <106575910+KRRT7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:15:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Live: never send the real face or a broken voice to the call

Vendored code changed: _vendor/modules/live.py and
_vendor/modules/processors/frame/face_swapper.py.

Face. A missed detection or a failed swap sent the camera frame
unchanged, so the other side saw the real face. Measured with the real
models on 720p frames with the eyes covered (the detector misses, the
rest of the face stays visible): 60 of 60 frames leaked before, 0 after.
- A miss shorter than FACE_LOSS_HOLD_S (0.5 s) re-swaps the face where
  it was last seen.
- Past that, or when the swap fails, the last swapped frame is sent
  again (a frozen picture) until the face is found; black before the
  first swap. Logged at most every 3 s with its recovery; exposed as
  FramePipeline/LiveSession.face_state.
- try_swap_face() and AsyncLiveSwapper.try_swap() return None when
  nothing was pasted; swap_face()/swap() keep their behavior.
- Off without source photos, in many-faces mode and for swap_image().

Voice. The converted voice never stutters, loops or clicks:
- A block the worker did not deliver in time fades to silence over
  5 ms instead of replaying the previous block (a repeated syllable);
  audio resumes, also after a dropped result, with a 5 ms fade-in.
- A dead worker means silence and voice_failed, not the last block on
  a loop; the Live log reports it once.
- A failing audio callback outputs silence, not the driver's stale
  buffer.
- The silence gate stays open ~0.3 s after speech, so a short dip no
  longer cuts the word and resets the conversion context.
- Late blocks are counted and reported with the other dropouts.
Real worker at 250 ms chunks with face swap running: 0 late blocks in
80; killing the worker gave silence after the fade, flagged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Applio-Commit: f32a51e6d352be4bebc14db0ea18921b2e807044
